 PingIndexNow registryPath;key;baseURL;stamp;ns;filename;lastPing;list;new;urls;url;maxUrls;qdmx
⍝ Tells IndexNow about the pages that changed since the last time it was told.
⍝ IndexNow is a protocol by which a site announces a changed URL instead of waiting to be
⍝ crawled. Bing and Yandex run it, and Seznam, Naver and Yep take part; Google does not, so
⍝ this speeds up discovery on some search engines rather than on all of them.
⍝ `OnHouseKeeping` starts this as a thread, so nothing waits for it, and only one runs at a
⍝ time. It traps everything for the same reason `ProcessReadmes` does: an untrapped error
⍝ would suspend the thread, and a suspended thread keeps its number in ⎕TNUMS for ever.
⍝ Two INI entries are needed. Without `CONFIG:IndexNowKey` the feature is off. Without
⍝ `CONFIG:BaseURL` it cannot work either: IndexNow wants absolute URLs, and a thread has no
⍝ request to work the public host out from.
⍝ The record holds `indexStamp` (the index file's timestamp when last announced), `lastPing`
⍝ (when that was) and `pinged` (how many URLs went out). No record means nothing has been
⍝ announced yet, and the first run announces nothing: it notes the time and stops, so that
⍝ switching the feature on does not fire off one URL per package in the Registry.
 maxUrls←50                                         ⍝ A publish adds one page; more than this is a bulk import
 :Trap 0
     :If 0=≢key←GetIndexNowKey
         :Return
     :EndIf
     :If 0=≢baseURL←⊃''G.INI.Get'CONFIG:BaseURL'
         :Return
     :EndIf
     baseURL←(-'/'=¯1↑baseURL)↓baseURL
     stamp←GetIndexStamp registryPath
     filename←GetIndexNowFilename registryPath
     ns←⍬
     :If F.IsFile filename
         :Trap 11 19 22
             ns←⎕JSON⍠('Dialect' 'JSON5')⊣⊃F.NGET filename
         :Else
             qdmx←⎕DMX
             LogError'Unreadable IndexNow record "',filename,'": ',qdmx.EM,'; RC=',⍕qdmx.EN
         :EndTrap
     :EndIf
     :If ⍬≡ns                                       ⍝ Never announced anything: start the clock, say nothing
         RecordIndexNowPing registryPath stamp 0
         :Return
     :EndIf
     :If stamp=⊃{0=ns.⎕NC ⍵:0 ⋄ ns⍎⍵}'indexStamp'   ⍝ Nothing published since we last looked
         :Return
     :EndIf
     lastPing←{0=ns.⎕NC ⍵:'' ⋄ ns⍎⍵}'lastPing'
     :If 0=≢lastPing                                ⍝ A record without one: start the clock instead
         RecordIndexNowPing registryPath stamp 0
         :Return
     :EndIf
     list←1 Reg.GetAllPackages registryPath         ⍝ [;1]=package ID, [;2]=publishing date
⍝ Both are "YYYY-MM-DD hh:mm:ss". They cannot be compared as they stand - characters have no
⍝ order in APL, only = and ≠ - so the punctuation comes out and what is left is a number.
     new←(({⍎⍵~'- :'}¨list[;2])>⍎lastPing~'- :')/list[;1]
     :If 0=≢new
         RecordIndexNowPing registryPath stamp 0
         :Return
     :EndIf
⍝ The pages that changed: one per major version line, plus the two that list what is new.
     urls←∪{baseURL,Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages/versions/',Reg.RemoveMinorAndPatch ⍵}¨new
     urls←(maxUrls⌊≢urls)↑urls
     urls,←baseURL,'/'
     urls,←⊂baseURL,Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages'
     :For url :In urls
         {}SubmitToIndexNow url key
     :EndFor
     RecordIndexNowPing registryPath stamp(≢urls)
 :Else
     qdmx←⎕DMX
     LogError'Announcing to IndexNow stopped: ',qdmx.EM,'; RC=',⍕qdmx.EN
 :EndTrap
 ∆INDEXNOW_TID←¯1
⍝Done
